@startuml task_content_mentions
!pragma layout smetana
title Typed projection task: content_mentions
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false

database "Unchanged outbox" as OUTBOX
participant "Task projector" as PROJECTOR
database "The subject line" as CLAIM
participant "The worker's slot." as WORKER
database "MESSAGE.payload" as MESSAGE
database "PLACEMENT + Users are tied up ." as ACCESS
database "USER_MESSAGE_STATE" as STATE
database "Typed tasks" as TASKS
database "Downstream outbox exact scopes" as FOLLOWUPS
database "The public events repository" as EVENTS
participant "The controller . WebSocket" as DISPATCHER
actor "The client ." as Client

OUTBOX -> PROJECTOR : event of message creation/change
PROJECTOR -> TASKS : immutable content_mentions(outbox_event_uuid, scope=topic)\nunique derivation; without coalescing
TASKS -> WORKER : Clearly waiting work
WORKER -> CLAIM : Monopoly capture of the topic
WORKER -> MESSAGE : Read the last canonical load
WORKER -> ACCESS : Read the recorded placements/receivers
group One . DB transaction
  loop the affected user/message
    WORKER -> STATE : I 'mpotent to insert or update the mention status
  end
  WORKER -> FOLLOWUPS : immutable outbox events:\nuser-stream / user-topic / user-folder
  WORKER -> EVENTS : durable ready topic-scoped rows
end
WORKER -> CLAIM : I 'm going to get out .
EVENTS -> DISPATCHER : - I 'm not sure .
DISPATCHER -> Client : Send / repeat / play

note over MESSAGE,STATE
  The payload remains in the only copy in MESSAGE.
  Status only saves personal flags,
  but not the stream/topic/folder aggregates.
  USER_MESSAGE_STATE key = (project,user,placement).
  Shared rows Only the owner can change it . exact scope key.
  Lease/fencing + retry/backoff + DLQ/reaper - They 're compulsory ..
end note

@enduml
